{
  "tolerance": 1e-09,
  "notes": "Per-m2 half of the portal Chl a tool tab (modules/tools_tab/tools/chla_tool.R). Replicates are looped exactly as the portal does (lines 279-438) and summarised by the portal avg/sd loop (lines 444-492), giving the portal column spellings chla_acid_ugm2_rep_X / chla_noacid_ugm2_rep_X / afdm_gm2_rep_X and Chla_acid_avg_ugm2 / Chla_acid_sd_ugm2 / Chla_noacid_avg_ugm2 / Chla_noacid_sd_ugm2 / Chla_acid_ugL_avg / Chla_acid_ugL_sd / Chla_noacid_ugL_avg / Chla_noacid_ugL_sd / benthic_AFDM_avg_gm2 / benthic_AFDM_sd_gm2. Every replicate cell is its own param named as the portal names the column (lab_chla_sizeA_rep_C, chla_acid_ugL_rep_C, afdm_g_filter_rep_C), so the replicate letter is carried by the field name and a blank cell cannot slide onto another letter. convertToUnitPerM2 is a three-axis formula and calcBenthicAFDM/calcChlaPerM2 refuse unless sizeA, sizeB and sizeC are all present, so a letter missing any one axis yields no per-m2 output for that letter. The portal's 'KEEP OLD' carry-forward (reuse the stored database value when a calculation cannot run) is deliberately NOT emulated: this tool is stateless, so KEEP OLD becomes an omitted key. A non-finite conversion is NOT filtered out: the portal's ifelse(x != 'KEEP OLD', ...) coerces a numeric x to a string, so an Inf survives into calcMean and calcSd rather than the mean being taken over the other replicates. The wrapper emits Inf and NaN like any other value, and the portal displays them; they serialise to JSON null and the API drops nulls, so they appear in these cases' absent lists (zero_volume_filtered_poisons_the_aggregate: rep A and both per-m2 summaries are Inf in the portal). NaN additionally converges with the portal inside calcMean/calcSd, whose na.rm=TRUE drops NaN and whose is.na guard turns an all-NaN result into KEEP OLD. Divergence from the previous API contract, recorded as the tool seed contract (workspace docs/tools/CONTRACT.md) requires: the request is the portal's five-replicate grid rather than the earlier flat single-replicate fields (diameters_cm, afdm_g_filter, chla_ug_l, volume_filtered_ml, total_volume_ml), and chla_ug_l is split into chla_acid_ugl and chla_noacid_ugl because the portal keeps the acid and no-acid families as separate columns (chla_tool.R:284-293). Two former output keys are gone with it: Chla_avg_ugm2 was acid-agnostic and is replaced by the portal's Chla_acid_avg_ugm2 and Chla_noacid_avg_ugm2 (chla_tool.R:444-462), and rock_surface_area_m2 is not a portal column at all, the area existing only as the local `area` inside convertToUnitPerM2 (calculation_functions.R:461). The earlier positional grid also carried two cases the named params cannot express and that pinned nothing about the arithmetic: four_axes_uses_first_three (there is no fourth diameter column) and sixth_replicate_has_no_letter (there is no rep_F param, and a request naming one is refused before the script runs).",
